<Solution>
  <!--
    The solution lives at the repository root, so opening the repository opens the
    solution, exactly as a template generated with the Aspire AppHost selected does.
    One `src/` holds every project the factory is made of and the host that runs it;
    one `tests/` holds both test projects. `docs/architecture.md` is the architecture
    of record for what the four factory projects are and why the AppHost is not one
    of them.
  -->

  <Folder Name="/Solution Items/">
    <File Path=".editorconfig" />
    <File Path=".gitignore" />
    <File Path="Directory.Build.props" />
    <File Path="Directory.Packages.props" />
    <File Path="global.json" />
    <File Path="README.md" />
  </Folder>

  <Folder Name="/src/">
    <!--
      **`DefaultStartup="true"` is what makes F5 run the factory, not the Web project.**
      It is the same attribute the Aspire templates' `.slnx` carries: an IDE that reads
      the solution starts the AppHost, so opening this repository and pressing run gives
      the factory under Aspire — the resource graph, the dashboard and the OTLP pipeline
      — with no per-machine startup project to remember. The AppHost is under `src/` with
      the factory rather than beside it, and `ArchitectureTests.TheFactoryProjects` skips
      it by name: it is a fifth *project* but not a fifth assembly the factory is made of.
    -->
    <Project Path="src/AgentFactory.AppHost/AgentFactory.AppHost.csproj" DefaultStartup="true" />
    <Project Path="src/AgentFactory.Application/AgentFactory.Application.csproj" />
    <Project Path="src/AgentFactory.Domain/AgentFactory.Domain.csproj" />
    <Project Path="src/AgentFactory.Infrastructure/AgentFactory.Infrastructure.csproj" />
    <Project Path="src/AgentFactory.Web/AgentFactory.Web.csproj" />
  </Folder>

  <Folder Name="/tests/">
    <!--
      Everything whose truth depends on the real composition, plus the fast layer over
      `Domain` and `Application` alone (#86). Which layer a test belongs to is decided by
      what its truth depends on; see `docs/architecture.md`'s Testing section.
    -->
    <Project Path="tests/agent-factory.tests/agent-factory.tests.csproj" />
    <Project Path="tests/agent-factory.unit-tests/agent-factory.unit-tests.csproj" />
  </Folder>
</Solution>
